From: Google Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-omap: use optional regulator lookup and preserve vmmc caps

1. When regulator_get() is used, systems with dummy regulators enabled
return a dummy regulator instead of an error. Because dummy regulators
do not report supported voltages, sdhci_omap_regulator_get_caps() computes
caps = 0 and clears all host voltage capabilities. Use
regulator_get_optional() so missing pbias/vqmmc regulators return -ENODEV.

2. If neither pbias nor vqmmc is provided and hardware CAPA has no voltage
bits set (e.g. an SDIO controller never initialized by the bootloader),
fall back to querying vmmc so SDHCI_CAN_VDD_* is populated cleanly.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-omap.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-omap.c
@@ -945,7 +945,7 @@ static unsigned int sdhci_omap_regulator_get_caps(struct device *dev,
 	struct regulator *reg;
 	unsigned int caps = 0;
 
-	reg = regulator_get(dev, name);
+	reg = regulator_get_optional(dev, name);
 	if (IS_ERR(reg))
 		return ~0U;
 
@@ -974,10 +974,16 @@ static int sdhci_omap_set_capabilities(struct sdhci_host *host)
 	vqmmc = sdhci_omap_regulator_get_caps(dev, "vqmmc");
 	caps = pbias & vqmmc;
 
-	if (pbias != ~0U && vqmmc == ~0U)
+	if (pbias != ~0U && vqmmc == ~0U) {
 		dev_warn(dev, "vqmmc regulator missing for pbias\n");
-	else if (caps == ~0U)
-		return 0;
+	} else if (caps == ~0U) {
+		reg = sdhci_omap_readl(omap_host, SDHCI_OMAP_CAPA);
+		if (reg & (CAPA_VS18 | CAPA_VS30 | CAPA_VS33))
+			return 0;
+		caps = sdhci_omap_regulator_get_caps(dev, "vmmc");
+		if (caps == ~0U)
+			return 0;
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * Quirk handling to allow 3.0V vqmmc with a valid 3.3V PBIAS. This is
